What this package contributes: the source-assisted complex word compiled at
cube size p = 10 (h = 20) instead of p = 11; four query modules for p = 10
(modules/: triple module p = 10, pair module n = 9, its centre-sharing
version with a 37th root, all-but-one module n = 8), each cut from a p = 11
module file by zero restriction and then annealed at p = 10 against the
exact compile ledger of the aligned word (README, "Modules"); the control
modules (PR168 v4's modules cut to p = 10 by module_cut.py); one frozen
compilation recipe applied to three module sets (layers/); the cube size as
a parameter of PR304's builder (aligned_word_p.py) and discovery driver
(discovery/make_layer_p.py); centre46.py (the centre-sharing graph); the
gauge-rank fix of PR233's maximum-weight pairing for h != 22
(discovery/pairs_mw_p.py); the record correction in aligned_word_p.py
(the births of gauges that PR194's source_aligned_local_v4.py drops are
removed from its record, so that PR200's checker can recount it); the six
resulting programs with their checks (verify.py). Everything else is
